    1                      ;=============================================================================
    2                      ;  22_branch_operand_hazard -- operands read in the ID stage
    3                      ;=============================================================================
    4                      ;  Branches and jumps resolve in ID, and two different things are read there.
    5                      ;
    6                      ;  The CONDITION (beqz/bnez/bltz/...) goes through decision_unit, which takes
    7                      ;  the zero/sign flags and, when fw_ex_id_rs1 is set, the EX/MEM flags instead
    8                      ;  of recomputing them from the register.  With the one-cycle stall
    9                      ;  hazard_detection inserts for a branch whose rs1 is still in flight, that
   10                      ;  covers every distance.
   11                      ;
   12                      ;  The TARGET of jr/jalr is the register VALUE, not a flag, so it needs its own
   13                      ;  path.  It used to have none -- branch_correction's mux_1 took register_in
   14                      ;  straight off the register file -- and a jr or jalr whose target register was
   15                      ;  written one or two instructions earlier jumped to the stale value.  decode
   16                      ;  now muxes register_in to the EX/MEM result under the same fw_ex_id_rs1 that
   17                      ;  already selects the flags, which closes both distances.  decision_unit keeps
   18                      ;  the raw RF_out1, so the condition path does not pay for the mux.
   19                      ;
   20                      ;  This file is what pinned that bug and is what proves it stays fixed.  Every
   21                      ;  case is written so a stale read is VISIBLE: the register is pre-loaded with
   22                      ;  a second, valid address, so a stale read lands on a block that records 0
   23                      ;  rather than silently re-running the setup and converging anyway.  That is
   24                      ;  exactly how the bug hid -- a jr to a stale 0 restarts the program, and an
   25                      ;  idempotent program then produces the right memory image on its next pass.
   26                      ;  Keep that property if you add a case here.
   27                      ;
   28                      ;  All seven words must read 1.
   29                      ;
   30                      ;  Result map:
   31                      ;    0 jr target, distance 1     1 jr target, distance 2   2 jr target, d 3
   32                      ;    3 jalr target, distance 1
   33                      ;    4 condition, distance 1     5 condition, distance 2   6 condition, d 3
   34                      ;    7 branch on a LOADED zero      8 on a loaded negative   9 on a loaded
   35                      ;      non-zero read from address 0
   36                      ;
   37                      ;  Words 7-9 exist because the flags stored beside a register have to describe
   38                      ;  the value that was WRITTEN to it.  For a load that is the loaded data, not
   39                      ;  the ALU output -- and the ALU output on a load is the effective ADDRESS.
   40                      ;  Each case is built so the address and the value disagree about being zero or
   41                      ;  negative, so taking the flags from the wrong one flips the branch:
   42                      ;    7  value 0        at address 128  (non-zero)  -> beqz must be taken
   43                      ;    8  value negative at address 132  (positive)  -> bltz must be taken
   44                      ;    9  value 1        at address 0    (zero)      -> beqz must NOT be taken
   45                      ;  Loads never forward into ID (forwarding.vhd cancels on RM), so all three
   46                      ;  read the stored flags, whatever the distance.
   47                      ;=============================================================================
